<mujoco model="ultrasonic_sensor_fragment">
  <!--
    RECONSTRUCTED FILE — this was included by main.xml (<include
    file="ultrasonic_sensor.xml"/>) but was missing from the uploaded
    project, so the simulation could not load without it.

    Rebuilt from how sim_node.py looks the sensor up:
        try:
            sensor_us = data.sensor("gripper_ultrasonic")
        except KeyError:
            sensor_us = data.sensor("ultrasonic_sensor")
    and from the existing <site name="ultrasonic_site" .../> already
    defined in gripper_body.xml. A MuJoCo rangefinder sensor casts a
    single ray along the site's local +z axis and returns the distance
    to the first surface it hits (or -1 if nothing is in range), which
    matches how vision_yolo_node.py and control_node.py both treat
    negative/out-of-range values.

    Please verify this matches what you originally intended (e.g. the
    site's local +z orientation should point away from the gripper body
    toward the workspace) before relying on it for the safety-zone logic.
  -->
  <sensor>
    <rangefinder name="gripper_ultrasonic" site="ultrasonic_site"/>
  </sensor>
</mujoco>
